== Part B: real git repos, real commits, real tags -- the pin/diff/compose wiring ==
-- building a throwaway platform repo: v0.1.0 (2.0.0 + 3.0.0 live), v1.0.0 (2.0.0 retired) --
-- building the matching throwaway ludlow repo: base pins v0.1.0, head pins v1.0.0 --

B1. retirement -> composed MAJOR -> the pull request check must fail (no cosign needed: the retired version has no evidence to look up)
REFUSE: composed bump is major -- ['2.0.0']
OK: retirement of 2.0.0 correctly refused the pull request check, comment names it

B2. resolved-commit mismatch -> refuse (ADR-0001's pin made load-bearing, bug #2)
REFUSE: platform tag 'v1.0.0' resolves to '7b3534be3c4778ef0cdd29189814e65c4cbae68f', but platform-pin.yaml pins commit 'cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc' -- refusing (ADR-0001's pin is load-bearing, not decorative)
OK: a pin naming the wrong commit for a real tag is refused, real git rev-parse caught it

B3. composed weaker than the publisher's tag (unchanged array, major tag jump) -> informational, exit 0, never lowers
INFO: composed bump (none) is weaker than the publisher's tag bump (major, v0.1.0 -> v1.0.0) -- informational only, never lowers what this institution treats as the obligation.
PASS: declared=major composed=none
OK: composed=none against declared=major (v0.1.0 -> v1.0.0) passes, prints informational, never fails

== Part C: real cosign verify-blob, invoked for real, against a deliberately-invalid bundle ==
-- a CHANGED version whose evidence file exists but whose bundle is not a real Sigstore bundle --
REFUSE: policy 3.0.0: cosign verify-blob refused the evidence signature (Flag --new-bundle-format has been deprecated, this will be the only supported format in future versions
Error: --trusted-root only supported with --new-bundle-format
error during command execution: --trusted-root only supported with --new-bundle-format)
OK: cosign (the real binary) was invoked against the invalid bundle and refused it; the gate propagated that as a hard refusal

-- a CHANGED version with no committed evidence file at all --
REFUSE: policy 3.0.0: no committed evidence/bundle at computed-semver/evidence/3.0.0.json[.bundle] for commit 8da4d0a6b25d18a7000d82fcd7caaa623084b7a6
OK: a changed version with no committed evidence file is refused before cosign is even invoked

== Part D: splice_body via the REAL CLI, with backslash-bearing evidence -- the exact re.sub() hazard ==
OK: first splice (append) survives backslash-bearing evidence, real CLI, exit 0
OK: re-run replaces the prior span in place, byte-identical, markers not duplicated -- real CLI, real re.sub(), backslashes and all

== Part E: cosign verify-blob is genuinely offline -- committed trusted_root.json, egress blocked ==

-- E1: WITHOUT --trusted-root, blocked egress -- must fail on the network, not on the signature --
Flag --new-bundle-format has been deprecated, this will be the only supported format in future versions
Error: setting trusted material: getting trusted root from TUF for new bundle verification: error getting live trusted root: failed to create TUF client failed to load metadata: tuf refresh failed: Get "https://tuf-repo-cdn.sigstore.dev/15.root.json": proxyconnect tcp: dial tcp 127.0.0.1:1: connect: connection refused
error during command execution: setting trusted material: getting trusted root from TUF for new bundle verification: error getting live trusted root: failed to create TUF client failed to load metadata: tuf refresh failed: Get "https://tuf-repo-cdn.sigstore.dev/15.root.json": proxyconnect tcp: dial tcp 127.0.0.1:1: connect: connection refused
OK: reproduced the reported bug -- no --trusted-root means cosign tries the network and fails closed when it's blocked

-- E2: WITH --trusted-root (the committed file), blocked egress -- must verify, no network attempt at all --
Flag --new-bundle-format has been deprecated, this will be the only supported format in future versions
Verified OK
OK: --trusted-root, egress blocked -- cosign verified successfully with zero network attempts

-- E3: WITH --trusted-root, egress blocked, WRONG key -- still a real, deterministic refusal, not a false accept --
Flag --new-bundle-format has been deprecated, this will be the only supported format in future versions
Error: failed to verify log inclusion: transparency log certificate does not match
error during command execution: failed to verify log inclusion: transparency log certificate does not match
OK: offline verification against the committed trust root still genuinely refuses a signature/key mismatch

